{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9ac8adba99b47ad5","type":"group","x":580,"y":340,"width":937,"height":1214},
		{"id":"f6f88fbfc3db9b8f","type":"group","x":2907,"y":-280,"width":963,"height":887,"color":"#9ad09e","label":"Only affects Procurement Agents"},
		{"id":"7349546ef9906fec","type":"group","x":2509,"y":-280,"width":392,"height":887,"color":"#ffd1d1","label":"User facing"},
		{"id":"f2a5f20ed476799c","type":"group","x":2509,"y":-580,"width":500,"height":194,"label":"Heads Up!"},
		{"id":"9553ea633ee7351f","type":"text","text":"## Executive Summary (AI Generated from error ridden notes)\nErrors are highlighted and must be corrected\n\nThis is a **hardware lifecycle management workflow** built around the Requested Item (RITM) record. It handles three primary scenarios when end users or technicians report hardware issues:\n\n1. **Fix** — Repair existing hardware\n2. **Replace** — Swap out hardware with available stock or new orders\n3. **Stock Order** — Proactive inventory replenishment\n\n---\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n**Entry Points:**\n\n- Portal submission (standalone request)\n- Incident-driven submission (RITM links back to parent INC)\n\n**Triage Step:** An agent reviews each line item on the RITM and sets a \"Fulfillment Action\" field, which then branches the workflow accordingly.\n\n---\n\n## Branch 1: Fix Path\n\n- Generates an Incident assigned to the technician\n- Caller = Requested For\n- Description auto-populates from the \"Fix\" line items and justification\n- Technician handles repair/shipping logistics independently\n\n---\n\n## Branch 2: Replace / Stock Order Path\n\nThis is the more complex flow and includes a PO generation script.\n\n**Sequence:**\n\n1. Gather line items marked \"Replace\" or \"Stock Order\"\n2. Check inventory against requested models\n3. Split into two sub-paths:\n\n| Inventory Status                   | Action                                                                                    |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **In stock**                       | Create SCTASK for distribution ==(no approval needed — already approved when purchased)== |\n| **Not in stock** (Models to Order) | Trigger approval flow → Generate POs grouped by vendor → Existing PO workflow takes over  |\n\n---\n\n## Notable UX / Business Logic Details\n\n**Approval Logic:**\n\n- Orders require approval with a detailed note: *==\"{assigned_to} is requesting approval to distribute (qty) {in_stock_assets} and purchase (qty) {assets_to_order} for {requested_for}\"==*\n- ==Distribution from stock skips approval entirely (rationale: already approved at time of purchase)==\n\n**SCTASK Assignment (Distribution):**\n\n- Assigned to the practice's onsite helpdesk queue\n- Fallback to EUC queue if no onsite queue exists\n- Agent confirms correct model is actually in stock before fulfilling\n- ==If wrong spec, agent edits the RITM with the correct model and re-triggers the order/approval flow==\n\n**Post-Order Follow-up:**\n\n- ==When RITM stage = \"Complete\" (PO received), an SCTASK is auto-generated to follow up with the recipient==\n- ==Assignment: If RITM was opened by an ITIL user → assign to them; otherwise → practice onsite queue (fallback EUC)==\n\n---\n\n## ==Proactive Inventory Management==\n\n==Separate from the user-facing workflow:==\n\n- ==Weekly inventory check against `cmdb_hardware_product_model`==\n- ==Models below threshold (where \"Pending Order\" is false) trigger a notification to a designated group==\n- ==That group submits a Hardware Procurement form==\n- ==POs are generated, \"Pending Order\" flag is set==\n- ==When PO is received, \"Pending Order\" is cleared==","x":-1740,"y":-420,"width":840,"height":2500},
		{"id":"68f4b7204d6e58c4","type":"text","text":"Is logged in user a u_oo_procurement_agent?","x":2580,"y":-260,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"9cb18da8dc926f23","type":"text","text":"Ordering for someone else?","x":3020,"y":-260,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7e954686da03f6fb","type":"text","text":"Treat as standard user\n(Must meet user criteria allow/deny)","x":2529,"y":527,"width":352,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c56dc699b57c345c","type":"text","text":"Treat as inventory user\n(See's entity's full catalog (except if OneOncology))","x":3414,"y":527,"width":436,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"35a239342e679f70","type":"text","text":"Is logged in user a u_oo_procurement_admin?","x":3020,"y":260,"width":250,"height":93},
		{"id":"b2b23d3400553580","type":"text","text":"Is selected company an ITSM practice?","x":3350,"y":-20,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5e78ea90f87daf16","type":"text","text":"Is selected company OneOncology?","x":3600,"y":180,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"851d7a62077c5362","type":"text","text":"# Filtering logic depends on two new roles:\n1. u_oo_procurement_agent\n2. u_oo_procurement_admin","x":2529,"y":-560,"width":440,"height":154},
		{"id":"6e69a2cf6b44fda1","type":"text","text":"Weekly inventory check, notify a group when model is below threshold > They submit a Hardware Procurement form.\n\nChecking table: cmdb_hardware_product_model\nFields: Threshold, Pending order\n==Notification fires for models below threshold where pending order is false==\n\nWhen the form is submitted,\n1. Give procurement_users ability to set fulfillment action on MRVS (to \"Stock order\")\n2. Generate POs\n3. Set pending order on models\n4. When PO is received, clear pending order on models","x":600,"y":360,"width":440,"height":520},
		{"id":"4842c82d0b426069","type":"text","text":"Approval flow for distribution from stock should be different than ordering.\n\nIf distributing from stock, an SCTASK goes to that practice's onsite queue (fallback on EUC queue)\n\nIn the SCTASK, the agent confirms that we do have the right model in stock. If so, they fulfil in the SCTASK\n\nIf an order is required (correct model was requested, but the user needs a different spec), go back and edit the RITM with the new model spec and trigger the same approval flow that would otherwise be triggered.","x":600,"y":920,"width":360,"height":614},
		{"id":"609a343b4d1331fd","type":"text","text":"Distribution from stock should not require an approval since those devices were already approved in order to be in stock in the first place.\n\n","x":1000,"y":920,"width":497,"height":614},
		{"id":"1db038a7c58fc2d4","type":"text","text":"# RITM\n- [x] **Parent:** INC or empty\n- [ ] **Stage:** Determining course of action","x":-271,"y":-380,"width":250,"height":240},
		{"id":"87ae866fd4507354","type":"text","text":"Agent sets \"Fulfillment action\" on each line item","x":-271,"y":-80,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f9e9cc1e90f01e62","type":"text","text":"# Provision Hardware\n**Conditions:**\n1) \\>= 1 fulfillment action in MRVS is \"Replace\" or \"Stock order\"\n2) RITM doesn't already have any POs related to it\n3) Approval is either approved or not required\n4) Item is listed in sys_property 'procurement_catalog_items'\n\n**Outcome(s):**\n1. MRVS rows where fulfillment action is either Replace or Stock order are grouped into an object array.\n2. Inventory is checked against those models\n3. Approval is requested on the RITM with detailed notes about what is being evaluated for approval.\n   i.e. \"{assigned_to} is requesting approval to distribute (qty) {in_stock_assets} and purchase (qty) {assets_to_order} for {requested_for}\"\n4. For each model where we have sufficient inventory, create an SCTASK to distribute assets from stock.\n5. For each model where we do not have sufficient inventory, create a PO for each unique vendor with the model listed as a PO Line Item","x":-100,"y":101,"width":580,"height":539},
		{"id":"abaf4b65bbc41ab7","type":"text","text":"Inventory check","x":-50,"y":740,"width":480,"height":60},
		{"id":"b8ebe86186c381c1","type":"text","text":"SCTASK: Order","x":-50,"y":879,"width":225,"height":60},
		{"id":"37cf705b4bc25531","type":"text","text":"SCTASK: Distribute from stock","x":205,"y":879,"width":225,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"1ae2a0b635266e2a","type":"text","text":"Approval flow","x":-50,"y":1020,"width":225,"height":60},
		{"id":"01ee426444950daf","type":"text","text":"SCTASK to provision in-stock item(s)\nAssigned to practice's helpdesk","x":205,"y":1020,"width":225,"height":240},
		{"id":"859a55176e550a60","type":"text","text":"Existing PO workflow\nAuto gen PO after approved","x":-50,"y":1160,"width":225,"height":100},
		{"id":"a268a093c2400f98","type":"text","text":"For orders:\nWhen RITM stage is \"Complete\" (because the PO is marked received) > Generate an SCTASK to follow up with order recipient make sure they know their stuff is delivered and that they don't need any additional assistance.\n\nConditional assignment:\nRITM opened by is itil > assigned to RITM opened by\nElse, assign to the practice onsite queue for the RITM's company\n(fall back on EUC group)","x":-255,"y":1385,"width":635,"height":299},
		{"id":"9132fbd0a7f3d59e","type":"text","text":"Form submitted (Portal)","x":-776,"y":-380,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"56f98fe58e268659","type":"text","text":"Form submitted (Incident)","x":-776,"y":-200,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3f9d6f2274c59d3f","type":"text","text":"# Generate Incident\n**Conditions:**\n1) Parent type is not INC\n2) \\>= 1 fulfillment action in MRVS is \"Fix\"\n3) Assignment group and Assigned to is not empty\n4) Justification field should populate incident description\n\n**Outcome:**\nAn INC record assigned to the agent with the RITM referenced in a \"Requested item\" field, the requested for in the caller field, and description pre-populated with the \"fix\" line items\n- [ ] ","x":-776,"y":101,"width":580,"height":539},
		{"id":"1ea8397aebc8f4c8","type":"text","text":"Technician arranges repair, shipping if needed","x":-776,"y":740,"width":580,"height":60}
	],
